Poor compliance, unable to cooperate with treatment.

Age: 18 to 85 years old (inclusive), with complete cognitive function and symptom description ability, and good compliance;
Confirmed by histopathology as gastric cancer or colorectal cancer, with TNM stage b-?c and meeting the criteria for surgical resection assessment;
No chronic metabolic diseases that affect autonomic nerve function and cardiovascular regulation (such as uncontrolled hypertension and diabetes);
National Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) classification <= Grade III;
Preoperative gastrointestinal motility assessment showed no organic or functional abnormalities.
Voluntarily participate in the research and sign the informed consent document reviewed by the ethics committee.
Those who have continuously used central nervous system inhibitors or psychoactive substances within 30 days before the operation, or have a history of chronic insomnia;
There is a history of language communication disorders or organic diseases of the neuropsychiatric system;
Combined with severe cardiovascular and cerebrovascular diseases, liver and kidney dysfunction or moderate malnutrition status (albumin 10% within 6 months);
Implantable electronic medical devices in the body (such as pacemakers, nerve stimulators, etc.) or metal prostheses;
Suspected or confirmed history of alcohol or drug abuse.
Other lesions that, based on the researcher's judgment, may reduce the possibility of enrollment or complicate enrollment, such as the working environment
Frequent changes and other situations that can easily lead to loss of follow-up.
Participate in other clinical intervention studies simultaneously.

NSCLC patient with EGFR sensitive mutation as confirmed by needle biopsy;
